                <pb facs="1337" n="1141" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1141"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Potsdam/7–2845</note>
                <head>No. 1150<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Polish
                    Delegation</hi></head>
                <p>Following what was declared by Mr. Byrnes,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1150-f1"/>
                    Chairman of the Conference of the three Foreign Ministers, that regardless of
                    oral declarations it was permissible to send in documentary materials in
                    writing, the Polish Delegation have the honour to transmit enclosed some papers
                    referring to the problem of Poland’s Western frontier, together with an opinion
                    of Professor Stanislaw Grabski, Deputy Chairman of Polish National Council.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Potsdam</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-28">July 28,
                            1945</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>








